+**What a field chooses when focused: `select:`.** Unsaid, the cursor goes to the end of what the field holds.
+`select: all` chooses all of it, so what is typed replaces it; `select: stem` chooses what is before its last dot, as a
+file manager offers a name to rename: `report.pdf` with `report` chosen (a name with no dot, or one that starts with
+it as `.bashrc`, is all chosen). It holds whether the field is focused by a rule (`focus name`) or by the logic.
+
 **A scene that ends: `quit`.** In a rule, `quit` ends the program, as closing
 its window would: a terminal whose last shell ended.
 
